    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-04T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Sources, licences and machine checks"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: All 125 cards: every German form, article, plural, English and Swedish meaning and note against the content sources and the verification sources; the builder's Wikidata checks."@en ,
                 "Outcome: Every card has evidence from a content source (Wikidata, the FSI course or the War Department phrase book) and from German and English Wiktionary; every Swedish back is also checked in Folkets lexikon. German Wiktionary agrees with the spelling, part of speech and article of every card, and with the plural of every noun that has a plural note. The builder's Wikidata checks cover the German, English, Swedish or mul labels and aliases of 104 linked items (253 checks); they all pass. Discrepancies between the sources and how they were resolved are listed below."@en .

<#review-1>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-04T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Factual accuracy"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: All 125 cards: German spelling, articles, plurals, English and Swedish meanings and notes, against the official Regelwerk 2024, German Wiktionary and a live run of the builder's Wikidata checks."@en ,
                 "Outcome: No card was found factually wrong; all 253 Wikidata checks passed. Two warnings: the front \"sein\" can also be the possessive \"his/its\", and the selection overstated that only words common to Germany, Austria and Switzerland were kept. Three suggestions: Liechtenstein in the Strasse note, the phrase book called a \"course\", and the vowel length behind tschüs/tschüss. Each finding was checked against the sources; the two warnings and the course wording were fixed, the other two suggestions declined."@en .

<#review-2>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-04T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Language, translation and language tags"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: All 125 cards: language tags of every text, German spelling and grammar, English and Swedish idiom, the study direction, and the description."@en ,
                 "Outcome: No errors or warnings: every text is tagged (de fronts, zxx digits, en and sv backs and notes), the German follows current spelling, and the English and Swedish are idiomatic. Three suggestions: the phrase book called a \"course\" and an ambiguous front-side sentence in the description, the dated Swedish \"Hur mår ni?\" in the gehen note, and Swedish syster also meaning nurse. All three were applied, the last in a form that has a CC0 source."@en .

<#review-3>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-04T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Licensing, attribution and documentation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: The licences and licence evidence of all seven sources, the deck's attribution, the method and queries, and the evidence of about 28 cards against live sources."@en ,
                 "Outcome: All seven licences and the attribution in the built deck were confirmed. The findings were in the notes and the documentation: one note closely followed a CC BY-SA definition and several note facts were supported only by verification sources; one locator was wrong; the phrase book was called a course; helper scripts were not recorded; two Wiktionary quotes came from the wrong sense; and the US-only scope of 17 U.S.C. § 105 was not addressed. Every finding was checked and fixed. Every note fact now has a CC0 or public-domain content source (Wikidata lexemes and items, the FSI course, the War Department phrase book), found by fetching the Wikidata entities again (query 15) and searching the FSI text (query 16); notes with no such source were rewritten or removed."@en .

<#review-4>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-04T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Re-check of changed cards and a sample (facts, language, documentation)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: The 13 cards changed in round 3 and every third card (positions 1, 4, 7 … 124), 51 cards in all, against live sources; the licensing paragraph and source records."@en ,
                 "Outcome: The review confirmed the round 1–3 fixes, the Wikidata facts, the FSI quotations, the language tags and the build. One error: the licensing paragraph and the phrase book's usedFor still said the phrase book was the content source for gute Nacht only, although since round 3 it also supplies the facts in the auf Wiedersehen and guten Tag notes. Two suggestions on auf Wiedersehen. All three were checked against the dossier and fixed."@en .

<#review-5>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-04T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Re-check of changed cards and a sample (facts, language, documentation)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: The card changed in round 4 (auf-wiedersehen) and every third card (positions 2, 5, 8 … 125), 42 cards in all, against live sources (42 Wikidata lexemes, FSI Unit 1, the War Department phrase book p. 17 rendered from the archive.org PDF, German Wiktionary); the builder's 270 Wikidata checks, the validator and the documentation."@en ,
                 "Outcome: The review confirmed the round 4 fixes, the sampled cards' facts, language tags and Swedish, the metadata, the CC0 decision and the build. One documentation warning: method step 8 still described the auf Wiedersehen note as giving its literal sense, which round 4 had withdrawn. Checked against the dossier and fixed."@en .

<#review-6>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-04T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Final full-deck review (facts and language)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: All 125 cards: German spelling, genders, plurals, English and Swedish meanings, notes, language tags, study direction, title, description, keywords, evidence, and a re-run of the builder's 270 Wikidata checks; the round 5 fix to method step 8."@en ,
                 "Outcome: No errors or warnings; the round 5 fix was confirmed. One optional suggestion on the gehen note's Swedish, which was applied."@en .

<#review-7>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Version 2: title, description and keywords in Korean, German, Spanish and French (AI)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: the deck’s title, description and keywords, translated by an AI agent from the English (the Swedish settling what was ambiguous) into Korean, German, Spanish and French, in the words the app itself uses, and checked by a second AI agent that translated every text back into English and fixed what had drifted; the release compared by a script with version 1, which found the new title, description and keywords and the release’s own metadata the only changes, and checked by the library checker; not a human review."@en ,
                 "Outcome: the title, description and keywords are in Korean, German, Spanish and French as well; no card changed."@en .

<#review-8>
    a prov:Activity ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "Version 3: meanings and notes in Korean, Spanish and French (AI)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Scope: every card’s back and note, the word’s meaning,, translated by AI agents from the English (the Swedish settling what was ambiguous) into Korean, Spanish and French, and checked by a second AI agent that translated every text back into English and fixed what had drifted; the release compared by a script with the version before, which found the new texts, the description, the languages and the release’s own metadata the only changes, and checked by the library checker; not a human review."@en ,
                 "Outcome: every back and note is in Korean, Spanish and French as well; the fronts, the English and Swedish meanings and the sources are unchanged."@en .

